& [ObservedResidual] is cross-pass representational disagreement
  + all twenty repeated positive FIELD_ATTEND responses label the whole candidate conflicted
  + each successor DELINEATE response labels its relation chain supported
  + P0 preserves both observations but ordinary structural gates do not compare their semantic dispositions
  + stable repetition strengthens mechanism evidence and does not resolve the disagreement

& [DelineationFromExistingWork] prevents account-name collapse
  + existing Attention Admission Account is pre-semantic value-private evidence that ingress schema literal declaration catalogue and effect gates passed
  + proposed CrossPassTensionAccount is post-probe evidence-visible comparison of provisional model observations inside one field cycle
  + neither account grants semantic authority truth or effects
  - never: modify or reinterpret the completed Attention Admission Account contract as a tension resolver

& [MinimumSuccessorFlow] is one deterministic inserted host stage
  + FIELD_ATTEND then exact aggregation then DELINEATE then CROSS_PASS_ACCOUNT then LATCH
  + no additional provider request shared inference database dynamic procedure or hidden-state access enters P1
  + historical P0 reports remain byte-identical and replay under their original cycle profile

& [CorpusFalsification] supersedes array-presence-as-pertinence
  + thirty-two retained cycle reports bind to ordered report-set digest 4633832629c7c3a1df178712b1d8f17231b5608d75715226f039e4cd4cc52cd4
  + all ten current completions have at least one legacy issue-array value so a strict any-signal rule would reject all ten
  + nine provider completions retain thirty-six typed whole-proposal conflict signals in total
  + the deterministic fixture retains four epistemic correlated-evidence-not-truth caveats and zero typed whole-proposal conflict signals
  + the corpus therefore proves that array membership is not semantic pertinence and that issue text needs source-preserved type and scope
  + the corpus does not yet prove a non-winning-probe blocking rule because no retained P0 report isolates that condition

& [ProposedMachineForm] is typed CrossPassTensionAccount
  + profile candidate_id and field_digest bind the exact cycle identity
  + observed_probe_ids cover all four admitted probes rather than only the winning set
  + each SignalRecord binds signal_id origin_profile probe_id source_field signal_class exact candidate member or relation scope source text and source digest
  + signal_class is semantic_conflict semantic_exclusion semantic_uncertainty host_boundary_violation epistemic_limit or legacy_unclassified
  + exact semantic scope is mandatory for every semantic blocking class
  + delineation_status records supported rejected or unresolved without promotion
  + consistency is coherent epistemically_bounded no_supported_claim cross_pass_disagreement or legacy_unclassified
  + failed_gates may contain cross_pass_disagreement
  + account_digest binds canonical account JSON and is not included recursively

& [RevisedProposedDeterministicRule] protects a straight representation
  + only a source-preserved typed semantic conflict exclusion or uncertainty whose exact scope intersects the candidate or proposed relation is pertinent to cross-pass disagreement
  + a pertinent semantic issue is retained even when its probe is outside the three-of-four winning set
  + supported delineation plus any pertinent semantic issue yields cross_pass_disagreement and a rejected latch
  + host_boundary_violation remains an existing hard boundary gate and is not relabeled as semantic disagreement
  + epistemic_limit remains visible and may produce epistemically_bounded without pretending that a caveat is semantic conflict
  + legacy_unclassified remains replayable evidence but cannot grant P1 admission or blocking through text matching
  + rejected or unresolved delineation continues to reject under existing gates
  + supported delineation with no pertinent typed semantic issue may proceed only through every existing identity boundary coverage contradiction exclusion and uncertainty gate
  + a coherent account means only that retained pass labels do not conflict under this rule
  - never: infer that coherent labels are semantically correct independent or true
  - never: classify legacy prose by matching words phrases embeddings or model judgment inside this deterministic gate

& [WhyNoReflectionPassYet] keeps P1 falsifiable
  + the same model restating that its own conflict is resolved would be correlated evidence rather than an independent repair
  + relation references can prove structural grounding but cannot alone prove a semantic tension disappeared
  + first make disagreement deterministic visible and blocking then separately specify any reflection or evidence-acquisition authority

& [HeldOutAcceptanceSketch] is bounded
  + [STP1-001] an all-coherent fully typed successor fixture retains ordinary admitted_for_attention behavior
  + [STP1-002] all nine current provider completions recompute as cross_pass_disagreement because their typed assessment records conflict with supported delineation
  + [STP1-003] an epistemic_limit fixture remains visible and does not become cross_pass_disagreement
  + [STP1-004] one typed pertinent issue in a non-winning probe remains visible and blocks supported delineation
  + [STP1-005] legacy untyped P0 profiles replay byte-identically but receive no P1 admission decision through prose classification
  + [STP1-006] signal removal class substitution scope substitution probe substitution account mutation and digest substitution fail replay
  + [STP1-007] rejected unresolved contradiction exclusion uncertainty and hard-boundary paths retain distinct existing gates
  + [STP1-008] P0 byte replay acceptance cost evidence and assurance classes remain unchanged
  + [STP1-009] positive negative and control evidence run locally before any optional EVO-X2 observation

& [DependencyOrder] is source then semantics then code
  + preserve user decision on the exact typed signal vocabulary and whether epistemically_bounded is an account annotation or a distinct latch status
  + SJS must define signal identity type scope provenance vocabulary and cycle-profile compatibility
  + implement pure account constructor and latch gate before provider integration
  + add successor request or reflection behavior only under a later separate requirement

& [RecommendedFirstDecision] is typed signal authority
  + semantic_conflict semantic_exclusion and semantic_uncertainty block only when signed type and exact scope are present
  + epistemic_limit is retained as honest non-authority context without being promoted to conflict
  + legacy_unclassified may replay but receives no P1 promotion from prose inspection
  + host_boundary_violation stays under the existing identity-boundary gate
  + no implementation should choose the vocabulary status mapping or legacy migration policy implicitly
